32: ## Responsiveness Rule
33: When developing UI components or modifying styles, you MUST ensure full responsiveness across web and mobile platforms:
34: - **Mobile-First**: Base styles should target mobile devices, with media queries for larger screens.
35: - **Flexible Layouts**: Use relative units (`rem`, `%`, `vw`, `vh`) and layout systems (Flexbox, Grid) instead of fixed widths.
36: - **Touch Targets**: Ensure interactive elements are at least 44x44px on mobile.
37: - **Testing**: Verify your changes at various screen sizes (320px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px) to ensure no overflow or layout breakage.
